What would make it runnable
Programmatic access to registry change history at scale, by one of:

an AACT account and a restore of monthly archived snapshots, compared version against version;
written permission to retrieve the public History of Changes pages at a rate the registry accepts;
a data release of registry histories from the registry itself.

Any of the three turns this into a design. The hypothesis, sample and analysis would follow the structure of P28, which uses the same registry fields that are reachable.
